Z||000000||MontanaFiero||03-13-2001||04:01 AM||||For those of you electronically minded... Has anyone found a way to turn the 85 MPH speedo into a 120MPH speedo? I want to eventually get the white gauge face kit (mostly because the backlight filters are new, not faded), but they only work on 120MPH speedos. I noticed a kit in the Big Book to make a 140MPH speedo, but that's overkill and takes away from accuracy as far as I am concerned (I'd like to be able to tell if I am going 25MPH instead of guessing somewhere in that little space between 20 and 30).<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg">   <BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- <I>project</I> &lt;&lt;||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||03-13-2001||10:34 AM||||Just buy the 120 speedo. It is plug n' play right into any Fiero. They are on ebay all the time.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||rogergarrison||03-13-2001||12:43 PM||||I used the 200 mph kit from I think Fiero Store kit. Once i did the soldering and adjustments i used a GPS to check it for accuracy. Then a friend whos a Franklin County deputy sherriff, checked it with his radar gun. its only a few miles off at 140, and a little below 40. not enough to make any<BR>big differnce. I set it to read correct at 75.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||03-13-2001||12:44 PM||||OOPS !!!!!!!!!!!<P>I used the 200 mph kit from I think Fiero Store kit. Once i did the soldering and adjustments i used a GPS to check it for accuracy. Then a friend whos a Franklin County deputy sherriff, checked it with his radar gun. its only a few miles off at 140, and a little below 40. not enough to make any<BR>big differnce. I set it to read correct at 75.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||03-13-2001||12:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TheFiero64:<BR><B>Just buy the 120 speedo. It is plug n' play right into any Fiero. They are on ebay all the time.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yep the Speedo is plug and play, but the tach will need some tuning if you going from a L4 to a V6.<BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery (Updated Weekly)</A>||||reg||14
